The fish exhaled a breath of cool rain and poured back a name for every wound: Courage for the living, Memory for the dead, and Hope for the future. When Liora poured the names into her jar, the forest exhaled as if releasing a long-held breath. The well’s hum grew steadier, and the night brightened with quiet purposes. Names do not heal by force, it learned; they heal by reminding us how to walk forward together.
